# Operations tools on the local stack (docker compose up --wait), through the gateway. Operations routes take only a
# bearer token, never the session cookie (AD-8).
# Get a token from the client-credentials grant (RFC 6749 section 4.4) as the operations machine user:
#   scripts/operations-token.sh
# and paste it into @token below. With curl:
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $(scripts/operations-token.sh)" http://localhost:8080/api/v1/operations/disputes/<disputeId>
# Raise a dispute first as a customer (disputes.http) and copy its disputeId into @disputeId.

@app = http://localhost:8080
@token = paste-the-operations-access-token
@disputeId = paste-a-dispute-id

### Read one dispute: 200 with the internal status, the stored snapshot and every stored event; audited as DisputeRead Succeeded
GET {{app}}/api/v1/operations/disputes/{{disputeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### An unknown dispute: 404 not-found; audited as DisputeRead Rejected
GET {{app}}/api/v1/operations/disputes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Not a GUID: 400 validation naming disputeId; not audited
GET {{app}}/api/v1/operations/disputes/not-a-guid
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### No token: 401 unauthorized with WWW-Authenticate: Bearer
GET {{app}}/api/v1/operations/disputes/{{disputeId}}

### Start review a submitted dispute: 200 with the operations view (status underReview); not audited
POST {{app}}/api/v1/operations/disputes/{{disputeId}}/start-review
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Escalate a submitted or under-review dispute: 200 (status escalated); not audited
POST {{app}}/api/v1/operations/disputes/{{disputeId}}/escalate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Resolve an under-review or escalated dispute: 200 (status resolved); the trimmed note goes to the customer's timeline
POST {{app}}/api/v1/operations/disputes/{{disputeId}}/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"outcome": "upheld", "note": "We've reversed this debit."}

### Resolve again: 409 action-not-allowed with disputeStatus resolved; audited as Resolve Rejected
POST {{app}}/api/v1/operations/disputes/{{disputeId}}/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"outcome": "rejected", "note": "Again."}

### Resolve with no outcome: 400 validation naming outcome, after the lookup and before the status; not audited
POST {{app}}/api/v1/operations/disputes/{{disputeId}}/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"note": "We've reversed this debit."}

### An outcome that is a number: the framework's 400 validation, before the lookup; not audited
POST {{app}}/api/v1/operations/disputes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"outcome": 1, "note": "We've reversed this debit."}
